Z||000002||p4n1c||02-22-2001||03:17 PM||||I'm not a major in history nor am I an expert but my take on the the value of history is that it <B>tries</B> and helps us not make the same mistake twice, and to help us, as a society, better ourselves.  <P>The history of the holocaust was and is still taught because it reminds us of the horror human beings can cause and to maybe help try and not let another atrocity like that happen.  Is it helping?  I think so, but that's just my opinion.<P>Now the big debate can be whether or not recording history is actually helping us.  There are anti-history groups out there trying to denounce the holocaust and destroy history books, you should look into them and see their impact on recorded history(which I think is very little), and to see what value they put into history.  Try to see it from two views, it may help your paper.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 02-22-2001).]||||reg||1
